### Phase B — Production security smoke (REST Client)
### Base: Railway production. Fill @email / @password locally — do not commit secrets.

@baseUrl = https://sheikh-travel-system-production.up.railway.app
@email = REPLACE_WITH_ERP_EMAIL
@password = REPLACE_WITH_ERP_PASSWORD
@portalPhone = +923001234567
@token = (paste accessToken from B1 after login)
@foreignTenantId = 2
@matchTenantId = 1

### B1 — Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### B2 — /api/Auth/me without token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/me
Accept: application/json

### B3 — /api/Auth/me invalid token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.value
Accept: application/json

### B4 — Dashboard without X-Tenant-Id → 200 (JWT tenant)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### B5 — Dashboard foreign X-Tenant-Id → 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{foreignTenantId}}
Accept: application/json

### B6 — Dashboard matching X-Tenant-Id → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/Dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{matchTenantId}}
Accept: application/json

### B7 — Dev seed anonymous → 401 or 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/seed
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### B8 — Public lookup → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lookup/timezones
Accept: application/json

### B9 — Portal send-otp → 200; body data.devMode must be false
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customer-portal/auth/send-otp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "phone": "{{portalPhone}}"
}
